  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 188, 'Let your phone stay silent for one meal and enjoy the food without checking for updates.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 189, 'Write the name of something you are waiting on and draw a small box around it, as a reminder that it is only one part of your day.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 190, 'Choose three things you can control this afternoon and give them your full attention.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 191, 'Find a sound outside, like wind, traffic, or birdsong, and follow it for one minute without labeling it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 192, 'Look back over this challenge so far and pick the to-do that helped most, then do it again today.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 193, 'When travel plans shift or a ride runs late, put on a song you love and let the delay be part of the trip.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 194, 'Write "maybe" next to three worries on your mind today, and notice how the word softens them.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 195, 'Pick one small decision at work or at home and make it without asking anyone else''s opinion.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 196, 'Spend a few minutes making something with your hands, a sandwich, a sketch, a fold of paper, without knowing how it will turn out.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 197, 'Write down three things that are uncertain right now and one thing about each that you are curious to learn.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 198, 'Give yourself a quiet moment in the morning to set an intention, not a plan, for the day.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 199, 'Let a question from a friend sit for an hour before answering, if it can wait.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 200, 'Picture the version of you from five years ago and tell them one thing that worked out they never expected.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 201, 'Notice a mood that changed today without you trying to change it, and write down how it shifted.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 202, 'Try a dish from a cuisine you have never tasted, at home or out, and be open to whatever you think of it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 203, 'Walk into a room and notice three things you had never noticed before.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 204, 'When a worry shows up during a task, say "noted" and keep going with what you were doing.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 205, 'Ask a coworker, friend, or neighbor how they cope with not knowing, and listen for one idea to borrow.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 206, 'Jot down three things you are hoping for and three things you are open to, and notice which list feels lighter.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 207, 'Sit outside or by an open window in the morning and notice how the day feels before you know how it will go.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 208, 'When a decision feels heavy, decide which option is easiest to undo, and lean toward that one.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 209, 'Choose one worry and give it a nickname, then greet it kindly when it shows up today.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 210, 'List what you will do in the next hour, and only the next hour, and let the rest of the day stay blurry.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 211, 'Let someone you trust make a small decision for you today, and practice accepting it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 212, 'At the end of the day, write "I made it through not knowing" and one example from today.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 213, 'Find a weather report from last week and notice how the days actually turned out compared to the forecast.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 214, 'Leave your schedule open for a spontaneous ten-minute break, and use it however feels right in the moment.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 215, 'Remember a time you were waiting for test results, a job decision, or a reply, and write how you got through the waiting.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 216, 'Picture a future you cannot see clearly, then picture yourself standing in it, steady and okay.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 217, 'Notice when you seek reassurance from the internet today, and count how many times you resist.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 218, 'Choose a new path through a park or neighborhood and let your feet decide where to go.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 219, 'Write the words "I can take the next step without seeing the whole staircase" and keep them nearby today.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 220, 'When you feel the urge to ask "are you sure?" today, ask once at most and let the answer be enough.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 221, 'Start a small project, a plant, a sketchbook, a jar of saved coins, without deciding how it will end.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 222, 'Hum or sing a song while you wait for something today, and let the waiting feel a little lighter.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 223, 'Write about a closed door in your past and the different door that opened afterward.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 224, 'Pick a small gamble with no real cost, like a new shampoo or a new walking path, and try it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 225, 'Notice whether you feel calmer after looking something up, or whether you want to look again, and write down which.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 226, 'Spend a few minutes in the morning noticing the temperature, the sky, and the sounds, before you check any news.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 227, 'Make a quick plan for tomorrow with just three items, and leave the order open.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 228, 'When a friend shares worry about the future, say "I don''t know either, but I''m here."'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 229, 'Write down what "good enough" would look like for one thing you are working on, and stop when you reach it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 230, 'Choose one thing to look forward to this week that does not depend on how anything turns out.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 231, 'Take a slow bite of food and notice its taste without planning the next bite.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 232, 'Name one thing that is changing in your life right now and one thing that is staying the same.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 233, 'Let a small problem stay unsolved until tomorrow, and notice how much it bothers you by bedtime.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 234, 'Look at the moon tonight and notice its shape, knowing it will look different in a few days.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 235, 'Write a list of the small surprises from the past month, the kind you only notice looking back.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 236, 'Try writing with your other hand for one minute and enjoy the wobbly, unpredictable letters.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 237, 'When a plan is canceled, give yourself five minutes to feel it, then choose one thing to do with the open time.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 238, 'Think about a goal and ask "What is the smallest step I can take without knowing if it will work?" Then take it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 239, 'Write one sentence that begins "I''m curious to see..." about something uncertain in your life.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 240, 'Notice how many decisions you made today without thinking, and give yourself credit for each one.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 241, 'Spend a few minutes in a garden, yard, or park, and notice one plant that has grown since you last looked.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 242, 'Before sleep, tell yourself "Tomorrow can be figured out tomorrow," and let your mind rest.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 243, 'Choose a route home that is a little longer but more interesting, and enjoy the extra minutes.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 244, 'Practice saying "I''m not sure, let me think about it" when someone asks you something today.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 245, 'Write down the worry that keeps coming back, and next to it write the very next thing you could do about it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 246, 'Make a cup of tea or coffee slowly, paying attention to each step, while a worry sits in the background.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 247, 'Cook a meal and change one part of the recipe on a whim, then taste the result.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 248, 'When you feel pressure to have an answer right away, ask for a little time and take it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 249, 'Remember a time a stranger helped you unexpectedly, and let it remind you that help can arrive unplanned.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 250, 'Write a gentle reply to the voice in your head that says you must know everything.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 251, 'Pick a small item to buy with a quick decision, and do not compare prices more than twice.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 252, 'Go outside at a time of day you usually stay in, and see what the world looks like then.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 253, 'Spend five minutes writing about a hope that you can''t promise will come true.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 254, 'Allow one text to stay on "read" for a while without explaining why you haven''t answered yet.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 255, 'Think of a time the weather ruined a plan, and recall one good thing that happened anyway.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 256, 'List three parts of tomorrow you are sure of and three you are not, and accept both lists.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 257, 'Finish one task with a "good enough" effort and move on without polishing it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 258, 'Choose a museum, gallery, or local landmark you''ve never visited and plan to go without knowing what''s inside.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 259, 'Ask a family member what they remember about a time of change in your family, and listen for surprises.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 260, 'Write down one thing you are trying to predict, then write "I''ll learn the answer when it comes."'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 261, 'Notice how your breath feels when you think about the future, then notice how it feels when you think about right now.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 262, 'Hold a small stone or object in your hand while you wait today, and use it as an anchor to the present.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 263, 'Try a new kind of movement outside, like skipping, a short jog, or walking backward for a few steps, and laugh at the wobble.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 264, 'Write about a time you made a choice without all the facts, and what you learned from it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 265, 'Let your evening plans form as the evening goes, rather than deciding them in the morning.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 266, 'When you feel tempted to reread a document for mistakes, read it once more at most, then send it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 267, 'Make a list of things in nature that thrive because of change: tides, seasons, rivers, migrations.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 268, 'Imagine you are a traveler in a new city today, and approach one familiar place as if you''ve never seen it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 269, 'Pick one question you have been asking others repeatedly and decide to stop asking it for today.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 270, 'Write a simple calming routine for waiting, three steps you can repeat, and use it once today.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 271, 'Watch a sunrise or sunset if you can, and notice how it is never quite the same twice.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 272, 'Ask yourself "What am I trying to guarantee right now?" when you feel tense, and loosen your grip a little.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 273, 'Try a new board game, card game, or sport where you don''t know the rules well and learn as you go.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 274, 'Write a list of what you would like to keep steady in your life no matter what changes.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 275, 'Leave your umbrella or jacket decision to the moment you step outside, rather than checking the forecast first.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 276, 'When someone else is late, use the time to notice your surroundings rather than imagining reasons why.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 277, 'Spend a few minutes reading about a part of the world you''ve never thought about, and enjoy how much there is to learn.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 278, 'Write about one thing you cannot know yet, and end with three things you will do today regardless.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 279, 'Choose a gift, card, or treat for someone without overthinking whether it''s perfect.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 280, 'Notice a moment when you felt the need to have the last word or the final answer, and let it go.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 281, 'Glancing back over this challenge so far, write down one way your relationship with not knowing has shifted.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 282, 'Give yourself permission to not have an opinion about something today, and say so if asked.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 283, 'Sit with a cup of something warm while it rains, snows, or blows outside, and enjoy being inside the weather.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 284, 'Choose a time today to step away from screens for twenty minutes, and see what you notice when you return.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 285, 'Write down one value and one action that matches it, then do the action even if the outcome is unclear.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 286, 'Notice one way you planned for the worst recently, and ask whether that plan helped or just added worry.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 287, 'Try a new hairstyle, outfit, or accessory today and see how the day feels in it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 288, 'Write "it''s okay to wait" on your hand or a note, and look at it the next time you feel impatient.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 289, 'Tell yourself "I''ll cross that bridge when I come to it" about one worry, and picture the bridge far ahead.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 290, 'Notice the first leaf, flower, or frost of a new season and pause to appreciate it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 291, 'Make a decision today by asking "Which choice would I be proud of, no matter how it turns out?"'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 292, 'Ask yourself what is waiting for you in the next ten minutes, and focus only on that.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 293, 'Pick one routine check you do every day, like the weather or your bank balance, and skip it once today.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 294, 'Write a letter you will not send to the part of you that wants every answer, thanking it for trying to protect you.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 295, 'Bring a small snack or a book with you today, so any unexpected wait becomes a bit of free time.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 296, 'Choose one thing you can''t fix and one thing you can, and spend ten minutes on the one you can.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 297, 'Say "let''s find out" instead of "I''m worried about" when you talk about something ahead.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 298, 'Notice a sound you can''t identify today, and let it stay a mystery.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 299, 'When you''re waiting for a reply, take a short walk and return before looking at your phone.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 300, 'Write down an old worry from this time last year and what actually happened.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 301, 'Plan a picnic, outing, or gathering with a simple backup if the weather turns, and stop planning there.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 302, 'Read a poem you have never seen before and let its meaning stay a little unclear.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 303, 'Hold off on forming a judgment about someone new until you''ve spent more time with them.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 304, 'Pick a small thing to learn today, a knot, a recipe step, a word, without knowing whether you''ll remember it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 305, 'When a worry visits at night, write it on a notepad by your bed and tell it you''ll meet it in the morning.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 306, 'Take a photo of something ordinary that looks different in today''s light, and keep it as a reminder that things shift.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 307, 'Make a choice at a menu, shelf, or counter within thirty seconds, and enjoy what you picked.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 308, 'List three things that would still be good about your life even if one big uncertainty went the wrong way.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 309, 'Volunteer to try a new task at work or home that you don''t fully know how to do yet.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 310, 'Notice how a plant, pet, or child handles a new situation today, and borrow a little of their ease.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 311, 'Write down one thing you were sure of ten years ago that turned out differently, and smile at it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 312, 'Sit quietly for three minutes and notice each thought that passes, without following where it leads.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 313, 'Treat one unexpected change today as a small adventure, and tell someone about it later.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 314, 'Leave a small gap between tasks today, five minutes, and see what fills it on its own.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 315, 'Write two possible answers to a question you are waiting on, then write one thing you''d do with each.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 316, 'Spend part of a lunch break sitting somewhere new, and notice what catches your eye.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 317, 'Remember a trip that went off plan, a missed train or a wrong turn, and recall a moment you enjoyed because of it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 318, 'Ask yourself "Am I solving a problem or trying to feel certain?" when you catch yourself researching.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 319, 'Make a short list of steady anchors in your week, people, routines, places, and thank one of them.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 320, 'Let a weekend morning start without a plan, and decide what to do only after breakfast.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 321, 'When a decision feels stuck, write the pros of each option for two minutes, then choose and stop writing.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 322, 'Find a quiet spot and watch the wind move through grass, branches, or water for a few minutes.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 323, 'Notice how much of today you could not have predicted when you woke up, and write down one example.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 324, 'Try a new route for your evening walk or drive, even if it takes a little longer.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 325, 'Say "I can wait" to yourself the next time you feel the urge to check on something you''re expecting.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 326, 'Recall someone you once felt unsure about who surprised you in a good way, and send them a friendly note if you can.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 327, 'Give one unopened envelope, email, or task a specific time today, and leave it alone until then.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 328, 'Spend a few minutes with a map of a place you''d like to visit, and imagine wandering without a set itinerary.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 329, 'Picture your worry sitting in a waiting room, and let it wait there while you do one pleasant thing.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 330, 'Choose a small way to be kind to someone today without knowing how they''ll respond.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 331, 'Write the phrase "I am safe enough right now" and read it slowly three times.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 332, 'Look for a sign of autumn, winter, spring, or summer outside, and notice how it arrived without any planning from you.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 333, 'Make a list of the uncertain things you got through in the past year, and read it aloud.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 334, 'When a waiting room, line, or traffic slows you down, roll your shoulders and soften your jaw.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 335, 'Ask someone for their favorite surprise from the past year, and share yours.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 336, 'Write one goal for the coming season and add "or something like it" at the end.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 337, 'Turn off notifications for one app or inbox this afternoon and check it on your own schedule instead.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 338, 'Choose a small problem and brainstorm three silly solutions before picking a sensible one.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 339, 'Notice one time today when you let something go instead of trying to pin it down, and write it in a notebook.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 340, 'Wander through a bookstore, thrift store, or library and pick up the first thing that catches your eye.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 341, 'When you think about the future, try to describe it in pencil rather than pen, and write one hope lightly.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 342, 'Remember a time you said "I don''t know" and someone respected you more for it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 343, 'Go to bed tonight with one question still open, and let sleep do its work.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 344, 'Write a list of things you don''t need to know today, and cross each one off with a sense of relief.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 345, 'Choose to trust one person''s word today without checking or confirming it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 346, 'Walk outside in the early morning or late evening and notice how the season feels at that hour.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 347, 'Pick one plan for the week and decide in advance how you''ll adapt if it changes.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 348, 'Try sitting with a mild discomfort today, a slow line or a quiet pause, for one minute longer than usual.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 349, 'Notice the curiosity hidden inside one worry, and ask the question that curiosity wants to ask.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 350, 'Write down how you hope to feel as you face the unknown, then do one thing that helps you feel that way.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 351, 'Let a friend pick the restaurant, the movie, or the walk, and be open to their choice.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 352, 'Spend a few minutes noticing your feet on the ground while you think about something uncertain.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 353, 'Choose one thing you''ll do today even if you can''t be sure it''s the right choice.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 354, 'Write a thank you to your past self for getting through a time when nothing was certain.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 355, 'When the mind asks for one more search, reply "I know enough for now" and close the window.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 356, 'Look at a forecast for the week and pick one day to plan nothing at all around the weather.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 357, 'Sit with someone you love, even briefly, and let the moment be enough without thinking ahead.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 358, 'Plan a small treat for the day you hear back about something you are waiting for, whatever the news, and put it on the calendar.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 359, 'Write about how a season in nature reminds you that endings and beginnings come in their own time.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 360, 'Take one small step on something uncertain, then pause and notice that you are still okay.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 361, 'Notice which of today''s worries were about things that hadn''t happened, and which were about now.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 362, 'Practice a short phrase for waiting, like "this too will become clear," and say it whenever you feel restless.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 363, 'Choose a small surprise for yourself this evening, a new song, a new path, a new snack, and enjoy it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 364, 'Write down three things this challenge has shown you about living with not knowing.'),
  ('making-peace-with-uncertainty', 365, 'End the day by saying out loud one thing you still don''t know, and one thing you are grateful for anyway.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 1, 'Before bed tonight, lay out tomorrow''s clothes, down to the socks, so the morning starts with one decision already made.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 2, 'Fill a water bottle tonight and set it in the fridge door where tomorrow''s hand will find it first.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 3, 'Plug in your phone, earbuds and any other gadget you''ll need tomorrow before you sit down for the evening.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 4, 'Wash the last few dishes and wipe the sink dry before bed, so the kitchen greets you clean in the morning.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 5, 'Look up when you last saw a dentist, and if it''s been more than six months, call or go online to book a cleaning today.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 6, 'Find your driver''s license and check its expiration date, then put a reminder in your calendar two months before it.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 7, 'Add the birthdays of three people you care about to your calendar, with a reminder a week ahead to send a card.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 8, 'Move a small, comfortable amount into savings today, even if it''s just the price of a coffee, and call it a gift to later you.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 9, 'Copy this month''s phone photos onto a computer, a drive or a cloud folder, so a lost phone won''t mean lost memories.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 10, 'Choose one spot in your home for keys, wallet and badge, and put them there tonight before you do anything else.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 11, 'Check the toilet paper, toothpaste and dish soap, and add whatever is running low to your shopping list now.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 12, 'Cook a double batch of something simple tonight and pack the second half as a ready meal for your busiest evening this week.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 13, 'Write a short, kind note to the person you''ll be tomorrow morning and tape it to the bathroom mirror.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 14, 'Check the forecast for tomorrow, and if rain is coming, set the umbrella right by the front door tonight.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 15, 'Pack your bag for tomorrow tonight: laptop, charger, lunch container, anything you''d hate to run back for.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 16, 'Gather your birth certificate, passport and Social Security card into one folder and write on the front what''s inside.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 17, 'Take a ten-minute walk after dinner as a small deposit in the account your future knees and heart will draw from.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 18, 'Write down one thing you learned today in a notebook you can flip through months from now.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 19, 'Make your bed before you leave the room this morning, so tonight you climb into something smooth and ready.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 20, 'Check your prescription bottles and request any refill that will run out within the next ten days.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 21, 'Look at what''s due back to the library this week and renew it or set it by the door to return.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 22, 'Set your coffee maker or kettle up tonight, so the first step tomorrow is just pressing a button.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 23, 'Write the date your car''s oil was last changed somewhere easy to find, and note when the next one is due.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 24, 'Put a pair of comfortable walking shoes by the door so tomorrow''s walk has one less excuse to skip it.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 25, 'Spend five minutes stretching your neck, shoulders and back, the parts that will ache later if you skip them.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 26, 'Learn how to shut off the water to your home, and write where the valve is on a card in your kitchen drawer.'),
  ('taking-care-of-future-you', 27, 'Turn your bedroom a little cooler and darker tonight, and set out anything that helps you fall asleep.'),
